  summary: `# 🧬 Rec Adv Bioscience #1.2 — Proteomics

## 🎯 Proteomics = study of all proteins in a system
- Genome → Transcriptome → Proteome → Metabolome
- Proteins = functional units (genes are blueprints)
- ~20,000 human genes → ~1,000,000 protein species (post-translational mods)
- Vet applications: biomarker discovery, vaccine development, host-pathogen interaction

## 🔬 Key proteomics techniques

### 2D gel electrophoresis (2DE)
- 1st dimension: isoelectric focusing (IEF) — by charge (pI)
- 2nd dimension: SDS-PAGE — by molecular weight
- Spot detection (silver, Coomassie)
- Pioneer technique, now less common alone

### Mass spectrometry (MS)
- **MALDI-TOF** — Matrix-Assisted Laser Desorption/Ionization-Time of Flight
  - Bacterial ID (clinical lab — minutes)
  - Spectra fingerprint matching
- **LC-MS/MS** — Liquid Chromatography-Tandem MS
  - Complex protein mixture analysis
  - Peptide sequencing
  - Quantitative proteomics (label-free, iTRAQ, TMT)
- **Q-Exactive, Orbitrap** — high-resolution
  - Top-down (intact protein) or bottom-up (digested peptide)

### Protein identification workflow
1. Sample extraction
2. Digestion (trypsin, etc.)
3. Separation (LC)
4. MS analysis
5. Database search (Mascot, Sequest, MaxQuant)
6. Quantification + statistics

## 🐾 Vet proteomics applications

### Biomarker discovery
- Bovine TB: serum protein biomarkers
- Canine cancer: CSF proteome
- Equine inflammation: SAA, haptoglobin
- Fish immune response: mucus proteome

### Vaccine development
- Reverse vaccinology: pathogen genome → predicted antigens
- Surface protein identification (SPI)
- Subunit vaccine design

### Host-pathogen interaction
- PRRS: macrophage proteome changes
- Avian flu: lung proteome
- Helminth: secreted proteins (ESP)

### Clinical microbiology
- MALDI-TOF in clinical lab
- Rapid bacterial ID (minutes vs days)
- Standard in modern hospital labs

## 🎯 Strengths + limitations

### Strengths
- Functional readout (proteins = doers)
- Detects PTM (phosphorylation, glycosylation)
- High throughput
- Quantitative

### Limitations
- Expensive (instrument $$$)
- Complex bioinformatics
- Sample prep critical
- Low-abundance proteins missed

## 🇹🇭 TH proteomics infrastructure
- **CU Engineering + Pharm + Vet** — collaborative platforms
- **Mahidol** — proteomics core
- **NSTDA / BIOTEC** — national platform
- **Pacific Proteomics, BSM Lab** — private services
- Vet-specific: limited but growing

## 📝 EXAM RECAP
1. ⭐ Proteomics = all proteins in a system
2. ⭐ MALDI-TOF = clinical bacterial ID standard
3. ⭐ LC-MS/MS = quantitative proteomics
4. ⭐ Vet apps: biomarker + vaccine + host-pathogen
5. ⭐ TH: CU + Mahidol + NSTDA platforms`,
